he variance of <span class=\"math inline\"><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"Y\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D44C TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>\nthat the regression function explains. Compute it for the distribution\nof <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"exr-lm-hetero-tautology\">@exr-lm-hetero-tautology</span>.</p>","file":"ch05-model-and-least-squares/01-what-a-model-claims.html"}